Act as a senior backend engineer and AI systems architect.

Build the complete backend for a hackathon project called **ReelReason**.

ReelReason is an AI-powered web application that turns long videos—podcasts, lectures, interviews, webinars, and presentations—into purposeful, ready-to-post vertical reels.

Unlike ordinary AI clippers, ReelReason does not simply extract random clips. It understands the creator’s audience, platform, goal, and tone; transcribes the video; analyzes the transcript; selects meaningful and diverse clips; explains why each clip was selected; generates hooks, captions, hashtags, and target-audience recommendations; and sends structured clip data to a rendering service for 9:16 vertical reel creation.

The product’s core positioning is:

> **ReelReason: From hours of content to reels worth watching.**

> **ReelReason does not just find clips—it decides which stories deserve to be told, and explains why.**

## Primary backend objective

Build a production-quality backend that supports this exact flow:

1. User uploads a long video or submits a YouTube link.
2. User provides creator context:
   - Platform: Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, TikTok, LinkedIn
   - Audience: Students, Founders, Developers, Creators, General audience
   - Goal: Views, Followers, Leads, Authority, Education
   - Tone: Professional, Bold, Funny, Educational, Motivational
   - Preferred clip types: Opinion, Lesson, Story, Emotion, Humor
   - Number of clips: 3, 5, or 7
   - Language: English, Hindi, Hinglish
3. Backend stores the project and video.
4. Backend extracts audio.
5. Backend transcribes audio with word/segment-level timestamps.
6. Backend cleans and splits the transcript into semantic segments.
7. Backend analyzes each segment using an LLM.
8. Backend selects 3–7 diverse, high-potential clips.
9. Backend generates for each clip:
   - Start and end timestamp
   - Clip type
   - Hook
   - Title
   - Caption
   - Hashtags
   - Target audience
   - Reasoning: “Why this clip?”
   - Scores: hook strength, clarity, audience fit, shareability, overall score
10. Backend saves clip suggestions in Supabase.
11. User can edit clip metadata.
12. User can request rendering for a selected clip.
13. Backend sends structured data to the Remotion renderer.
14. Backend tracks render status.
15. Backend stores and returns the final rendered MP4 URL.
16. User can download the final reel.

