## Row Level Security

Enable Row Level Security on every user-owned table.

Implement policies so that:

- Users can read only their own projects, transcripts, segments, clips, reels, feedback, and logs.
- Users can create projects only for themselves.
- Users can update only their own projects and clips.
- Users cannot read or modify another user’s data.
- Backend service-role operations can bypass RLS securely for processing tasks.

Example policy pattern:

```sql
alter table public.video_projects enable row level security;

create policy "Users can view own projects"
on public.video_projects
for select
using (auth.uid() = user_id);

create policy "Users can insert own projects"
on public.video_projects
for insert
with check (auth.uid() = user_id);

create policy "Users can update own projects"
on public.video_projects
for update
using (auth.uid() = user_id);

create policy "Users can delete own projects"
on public.video_projects
for delete
using (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

Apply similar policies to:

- transcripts
- transcript_segments
- clip_suggestions
- rendered_reels
- clip_feedback
- job_logs

